ents/3368498179","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109170#issuecomment-3368498179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109170","id":3368498179,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IxzQD","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-04T19:40:26Z","updated_at":"2025-10-04T19:44:44Z","body":"> Not sure when I what I changed before the errors appeared. The errors are so general, that I can only suggest and I haven't found the cause yet. **It'd be really cool if someone can help out here to get to the root of this issue! :)**\n\n@Achtbitte check out my comment above yours. Did you ever change/replace the PNG/images in the tileset?\n\nI had to manually edit the .tres file of my tileset to remove the bad tiles. Another way to do it (maybe) is expand the PNG to be big enough to show the bad tiles, then delete them with the Godot UI, then restore the PNG to the original\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3368498179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3368529648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109170#issuecomment-3368529648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109170","id":3368529648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ix67w","user":{"login":"Achtbitte","id":236067141,"node_id":"U_kgDODhIZRQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236067141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte","html_url":"https://github.com/Achtbitte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-04T20:45:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-04T20:45:49Z","body":"Thank you for your suggestion!\nI indeed tested that out already. I have about 6 different TileSets. Not sure which one causes the error, but obviously I resumed it must be one of the ones recently rearranged a couple of times.\nSo I resized the recents to be really big and even created single tiles for the entire space possible in the image (to top it off, even with all of my used TileSets later on).\nThat did not resolve the issue so far.\n\nDo you remember seeing anything visible on your map indicating missing Tiles back then?\nI can't see anything that brings me further yet.\n\nTest 2:\nI deleted my TileSet atlases in a game backup one by one with Godot restart every time to see if the errors were still there. No difference, even with the atlases deleted the errors appear.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3368529648/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369311440","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109170#issuecomment-3369311440","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109170","id":3369311440,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7I05zQ","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-05T20:34:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-05T20:40:05Z","body":"Maybe they're still in the tile layers themselves? \n\nI never personally used the Godot UI to find bad tiles, that was a suggestion on my part, but looks like I was mistaken!\n\nI recommend opening relevant .tscn/.tres files with an external text editor and searching for the bad coords. Then you can work backwards from there checking IDs to see the owner. Then delete the entries w/bad coords if you're confident. It's not a lot of fun to do but that's how I got rid of the errors. \n\nIf you have a recursive directory text scanning tool, you can use that to search for bad coords, and more than likely there will be some that are unique to one atlas, and you'll know that is the problem tile atlas","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369311440/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3374522857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109170#issuecomment-3374522857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109170","id":3374522857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JIyHp","user":{"login":"Achtbitte","id":236067141,"node_id":"U_kgDODhIZRQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236067141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte","html_url":"https://github.com/Achtbitte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Achtbitte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-06T22:43:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T22:43:58Z","body":"I think your idea might actually work.\nI opened the respective .tres file in a text editor and looked up some coords. Lots of shared matches, so I went to Godot and there was actually one TileSet I found  looking through the Atlas coords that was the single one not having a tile at one of the listed error coords. Still, creating tiles at some of these did not lessen the amount of errors, so it was a wrong lead.\n\nNow, when there was this single one TileSet not matching listed coords and fiddling with that didn't work, my conclusion is - it has to be a TileSet I deleted already. I'm surprised that this is possible, but it's the only explanation I can find here.\n\nMaybe with the text editor I would be able to see a dead entry within these lines, but do I remember the name of a deleted sheet? Even my brain deleted that one. So, unfortunately I can't see anything else that brings me further.\n\nIt's a lot of manual work obviously - thank you anyway for being helpful here, dear one being naturally intelligent :D.\n\nIt's not so pleasant to be flooded with errors when opening my project, but it seems less struggle and timely effort to wait for a Godot update that provides us with a simple solution to that kind of nuisance.\n_Maybe more descriptive errors, or a PURGE invalid tiles button..._ ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3374522857/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0